      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3575832480,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "This is a minor thing (that already is all over this ttl wiretap module and shouldn't hold up this MR), but for the various `*err_info` strings that are presented to the user in the GUI pop-up, I'm not sure it makes sense to put the entire function name in the error as opposed to just the name of the file format/module. The pcapng module just puts: \"pcapng\". I think ordinary users may care about what file format failed to process the file, but not the function name.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
